      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright© 2017, International Institute of Anticancer Research (Dr. George J. Delinasios), All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "Label": "AIM",
            "content": "We evaluated the metabolic characteristics of small-sized lung cancer using 18F-fluorodeoxyglucose positron-emission tomography/computed tomography (18F-FDG PET/CT) with regard to programmed cell death ligand 1 (PD-L1) expression."
          },
          {
            "Label": "MATERIALS AND METHODS",
            "content": "PD-L1 expression was evaluated by immunohistochemistry with the antibody clone SP142 in 263 patients with surgically resected primary small-sized lung cancer. Specimens with <5% tumor membrane staining were considered negative. We examined the association between the frequency of PD-L1 expression and the maximum standardized uptake value (SUVmax) in preoperative 18F-FDG PET/CT."
          },
          {
            "Label": "RESULTS",
            "content": "Among patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC), the SUVmax was significantly higher in those with PD-L1 expression than in those without (p<0.0001). However, there was no correlation between SUVmax and PD-L1 expression in patients with neuroendocrine tumors (p=0.9638). Multivariate analysis revealed that smoking and a high SUVmax were independent predictors of PD-L1 expression."
          },
          {
            "Label": "CONCLUSION",
            "content": "PD-L1 expression was related to high glucose metabolism in small-sized NSCLC."
          }
        ]
      },
